<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24003" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-structĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a constructing</i>, <i>erecting</i>, <i>building.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: novi balinei, Trajan. ad <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep.
				10, 35</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tubulorum in cloacas,</span>”
				i. e. <i>a sinking into</i>, <i>insertion</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 5,
					9</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>an arranging</i>,
				<i>planting</i>, <i>setting in
			array</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">signorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Caec. 15, 43</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Front. Strat. 2, 3, 4</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">militum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Auct. Her. 3, 10, 18</span></i>
			.—In plur.,
				<i><span class="en">Amm. 28, 1</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>instruction</i>
			(syn.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">doctrina, institutio, disciplina): futuri
					temporis pro instructione (al. per structionem),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 5, 167</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
